    {
      "id": "2071204003380142279",
      "text": "A lot of people using Figma Motion still don’t know about anchor point control and path-based object animation.\n\nAnd honestly, those 2 things alone can make your motion feel way more intentional.\n\nMost people just animate from point A to point B.\n\nBut once you understand how to:\n\n- rotate an object from a specific anchor point\n​- make an object feel like it’s moving along a path\n- fake path animation even when it’s not natively there\n\nHere's a quick breakdown on how to do both in Figma Motion.\n\nIf you’ve been using Motion but haven’t explored anchor points or path-style movement yet, you’re probably missing some of its most useful capabilities.",
      "author": {
        "id": "2986849109",
        "name": "Asaad Mahmood - The Small Square",
        "screenName": "AsaadMahmood5",
        "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/1654861113979461632/wY36FZ6J_normal.jpg",
        "verified": true
      },
      "metrics": {
        "likes": 141,
        "retweets": 12,
        "replies": 5,
        "quotes": 1,
        "views": 7717,
        "bookmarks": 186
      },
      "createdAt": "Sun Jun 28 12:08:10 +0000 2026",
      "createdAtLocal": "2026-06-28 20:08",
      "createdAtISO": "2026-06-28T12:08:10+00:00",
      "media": [
        {
